      <package fileName="TGScripts_repository.tar.gz" sha1="69f0448f817b0dd70279c603645fe5a8b4ffc91d" type="script" releaseDate="20261119">
         <title>
            TGScripts - Astro Bucket List 0.47.0
         </title>
         <remove>
            src/scripts/TGScripts
            doc/scripts/AberrationInspectorTG
            doc/scripts/AberrationSpotterTG
            doc/scripts/AstroBucketList
            doc/scripts/BBStarReduction
            doc/scripts/ColorMaskTG
            doc/scripts/CSTG
            doc/scripts/DarkStructureEnhanceTG
            doc/scripts/DeconvolutionPreviewTG
            doc/scripts/LinearMasterBlend
            doc/scripts/LocalSupportMask
            doc/scripts/LRGBDeconvolutionMatch
            doc/scripts/ROILinearFit
            doc/scripts/StarSpikeProtectionMask
            doc/scripts/SubframeQualityReview
            doc/scripts/TGScriptSkeleton
            doc/scripts/EmissionLineIntegrationTG
            doc/scripts/TGFieldMosaic
            doc/scripts/TGCornerMosaic
            doc/scripts/TGHueRangeMask
            doc/scripts/TGDustContrast
            doc/scripts/TGPSFComparison
         </remove>
         <description>
            <p>
               Astro Bucket List 0.47.0 adds separate Moon-separation limits for broadband and narrowband targets. Each band can inherit the observing site’s default or use its own limit. New sites start with a minimum target altitude of 0°.
            </p>
            <p>
               Observing night now shows targets with at least 60 minutes of usable time by default. Set the minimum from 0 to 1440 minutes across all imaging windows for the night. Zero accepts any positive duration. The usable-target count, filter, exports and list actions use the same minimum.
            </p>
            <p>
               Rank targets by two criteria, including the start and end of the longest usable window. The altitude chart defaults to one hour before dusk through one hour after dawn, with adjustable margins and a full-day option. A blue Sky strip marks site darkness, while green and muted red distinguish usable and blocked time for the selected target.
            </p>
            <p>
               Observing controls now collapse together. A single message box below the chart combines the night summary, target details and hover readout.
            </p>
            <p>
               Copyright (c) 2026 Dr. Thorsten Glebe. All Rights Reserved.
            </p>
         </description>
      </package>
   </platform>
</xri>
